{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run && head -c 2500 draft/update47.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"Adds the compaction rule as a cited anchor for the registered question's analysis, so the claim that trimming cannot be the reason a joiner misses the corrective entry rests on a source range rather than on prose.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"src_compaction_trailing\",\n      \"file\": \"snapshot.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 217,\n      \"end_line\": 250,\n      \"kind\": \"code_observation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"interpretations\": [\n    {\n      \"investigation_id\": \"dec7dd4ba25743138e52303340152c0c-question-0\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src_snapshot_carries_config\",\n        \"src_restore_snapshot_config\",\n        \"src_process_config_entry\",\n        \"src_compaction_trailing\",\n        \"src_follower_append_entries\",\n        \"src_quorum_size\",\n        \"src_commitment_from_config\"\n      ],\n      \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n      \"defect_claim\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"Successor account for the registered propagation question, adding the compaction anchor for the claim that trimming cannot hide the corrective entry. compactLogsWithTrailing computes the highest index it may delete as min(snapshot index, last log index minus TrailingLogs) and deletes only up to it, with the comment that this ensures at least TrailingLogs entries and does not allow logs after the snapshot to be removed (snapshot.go:217-250). Combined with the install path, which sets the joiner's configuration from the snapshot's own configuration and index and sets its lastApplied and lastSnapshot to the snapshot's last log index (raft.go:1880-1975), and with the scan of entries above that index that updates the joiner's tracked configuration for any configuration entry in that range (raft.go:1595-1620), the analysis is: a stale snapshot whose corrective entry lies above its index is corrected as those entries arrive, and a stale snapshot whose corrective entry lies below its index - the case of a node whose tracked committed configuration is the stale one and which snapshots again, since takeSnapshot writes the tracked committed configuration and index (snapshot.go:155-190) - leaves the joiner with the stale membership, because compaction never removes entries after the snapshot and therefore cannot be the reason the joiner sees no correcting entry: the correcting entry simply lies below the snapshot the joiner installed. The question remains open by observation rather than by mechanism: no receipt in this run ships a snapshot to a joiner.\",\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"Every step of ","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
