y writer of the tracked configuration state, which is too strong - restoreSnapshot installs the newest local snapshot's committed configuration (api.go:677-678), installSnapshot installs the metadata of a streamed snapshot (raft.go:1960-1961), appendConfigurationEntry records the configuration it appends on the leader (raft.go:1238), and the conflict path in appendEntries rolls the latest configuration back to the committed one (raft.go:1548) - while processConfigurationLogEntry remains the writer for entries taken from the log, called from appendEntries and from the startup scan. The mechanism the account relies on is unchanged and in fact sharpened: the startup inputs are the snapshot's configuration and the log scan, and the scan's lower bound is what the feature moves. Extension note: this successor cites the repeat of the two-voter probe (receipt 0abdaee65d5d40159726504b73daa195), which returns the same split as the first execution, so the boundary that a node recovering without a configuration still votes rests on two runs; the account's other parts are unchanged. Extension note: this successor cites the two-voter probe (receipt b999288258be402cb987482ced5256c1), which shows that a node recovering without a configuration still grants a vote to a healthy peer while never becoming a candidate itself; the account's other parts are unchanged. Extension note: this successor cites the revised authority experiment (receipt 67fc59b525e54d01b709a19592689357), whose harness keeps committing until the caller's store reports a non-zero persisted commit index before restarting the node; the witness reappeared under that explicit premise and the account's other parts are unchanged. Extension note: this successor reports the repeat of the multi-node experiment (receipt fe822d82c6264158826e0303b4ce59b1), which reproduced the commit-rule, durable-snapshot and availability cases with identical operands but not the authority witness, because the caller's persisted commit index was zero in that execution and the startup scan therefore recovered the configuration; the authority paragraph now states that precondition and the counterevidence records it. A revised experiment that holds the precondition explicitly is submitted with this batch. Extension note: this successor adds receipt 4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332, which observes in a three-voter group that a node recovering without a configuration never attempts candidacy while the same node and log with the replay disabled do; the sources, the three earlier executions, the knowledge uses, the conclusion and the remaining counterevidence are otherwise unchanged, and the counter about the observation window is strengthened with the new control's sample counts. Correction note: this successor differs from the previous account of this question only by a transcribed latency; the control's election is now stated as the receipt records it (19 polls at a 5ms interval, about 95ms), not from an earlier construction run. Everything else - sources, executions, knowledge uses, counterevidence and limitations - is unchanged. Recovery. Receipt 9a373c13725a42aa9f48f59c0f2f2f1c restarted four real single-voter prefixes on their retained stores with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs on and off: with the flag on and no snapshot the node recovered an empty configuration (event 2: no members at index 0, 268 polls without a leader) although its log holds the bootstrap configuration entry at index 1 (event 0), the flag-off control on the same prefix shape tracked that entry and elected itself (event 6), and with a snapshot taken before a committed AddNonvoter the flag-on node kept the snapshot's index-1 configuration instead of the log's committed index-7 configuration (events 10, 11) while the flag-off control recovered index 7 (event 15). Source side the mechanism is settled: restoreFromCommittedLogs stores the persisted commit index and calls processLogs with it (api.go:723-754), advancing lastApplied before NewRaft runs the scan that rebuilds tracked configuration state from max(snapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1 (api.go:602-621), so committed configuration entries at or below that bound never reach processConfigurationLogEntry (raft.go:1605-1624) and the FSM's ConfigurationStore is never read back. That state decides election eligibility (raft.go:225-246), quorum size (raft.go:1085-1094), the leader's commitment membership (raft.go:456-467, commitment.go:35-64) and vote admission. First consequence: receipt 79a9cc34b3ce42e197c384775efecc3a removed server C from {A,B,C} (event 2: committed conf\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
